  "goodToKnow": "Die Hauptverhandlung is the main trial in German criminal procedure, after the Ermittlungsverfahren (investigation) and the court's decision to admit the charges. It's generally public, with witnesses heard directly, and ends with die Urteilsverkündung (pronouncement of the verdict). Germany has no jury; professional judges sit with Schöffen (lay judges) in many courts. Plural: die Hauptverhandlungen."
